<title>FINLAND: Finnish Jan EU-harmonised CPI rises 0.9 pct -SF.</title>
<headline>Finnish Jan EU-harmonised CPI rises 0.9 pct -SF.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Finnish consumer price index partially harmonised to European Union standards rose 0.9 percent year-on-year in January after a revised 1.7 percent rise (from 1.5 pct) in December, Statistics Finland (SF) said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>				Jan 1997	Dec 1996	Jan 1996</p>
<p> Yr/Yr			+0.9 pct	 +1.7 pct     +0.8 pct</p>
<p> Mth/Mth		    -0.1 pct	  0.0 pct	0.5 pct</p>
<p> Index (base 1994=100)   100.1	    100.2	  101.3</p>
<p>According to SF's regular national method of calculation, Finnish consumer prices fell 0.1 percent month-on-month in January and they rose 0.6 percent year-on-year, it said.</p>
<p>				Jan 1997	Dec 1996    Jan 1996</p>
<p> Yr/yr			+0.6 pct	 +0.8 pct   +0.5 pct</p>
<p> Mth/mth		    -0.1 pct	 +/-0 pct    0.2 pct</p>
<p> Index (base 1990=100)   112.6	    112.7	112.0</p>
<p>Six economists' average forecast for the national CPI figure was for a 0.8 percent rise year-on-year and a 0.3 percent rise month-on-month.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358 - 9 - 680 50 245</p>
